---
import BaseHead from "/src/components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "/src/components/sections/Header.astro";
import Footer from "/src/components/sections/Footer.astro";
import Projects from "/src/components/sections/Projects.astro";
import HeroSection from "/src/components/sections/HeroSection.astro";
import GlowLineSeparator from "/src/components/ui/separator/GlowLineSeparator.astro";
---


<html lang="en" data-theme="dark" class="dark">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title="Project 5: Discord Squash & Stretch Animations" description="Project 5" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <HeroSection title="Discord Squash & Stetch Animations" subtitle="4 short animations for the brand, Discord, using the animation principle, squash and stretch." />
      <GlowLineSeparator />
      <div class="project-content">
        <div class="hero-images">
          <video src="/project-5-video-1.mp4" controls></video>
          <video src="/project-5-video-2.mp4" controls></video>
          <video src="/project-5-video-3.mp4" controls></video>
          <video src="/project-5-video-4.mp4" controls></video>
        </div>
      <p>This design was created for my Motion Design class. The goal of this project was to create 4 short animations for a social media, based around a fashion, automotive, digital device, non-profit organization or any industry or brand we were interested in.
        Along with this, we needed to use an animation principle for all 4 animations. I chose to do discord for my brand, with my animation principle being squash & stretch.
        To have more freedom while animating, I recreated the discord logo within illustrator so I could change their eyes, and as a result, their expressions within the animations, giving them more life.
      </p>
      </div>
      <GlowLineSeparator />
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
.hero-images{
  max-width: max-content;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction:row;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
video {
  display: block;
  margin-left: auto;
  margin-right: auto;
  padding: 2rem 0 3rem 0;
  width: 40%; /* Optional: adjust as needed */
}
</style>